<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 09:11:35 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Africa</category><title>France-Morocco rapprochement overshadowed by fresh Pegasus spying claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260718-france-morocco-rapprochement-overshadowed-by-fresh-pegasus-spying-claims</link><description>
As France seeks to rebuild ties with Morocco after years of diplomatic tensions, a new investigation claims Moroccan intelligence targeted senior French officials with Israeli-made Pegasus spyware. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c93201a-81df-11f1-8ec7-d771ed8df869</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:42:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8d165700-81ea-11f1-816a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36L48Q4.jpg">AFP - LUDOVIC MARIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>As gang violence expands, Haiti's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260718-as-gang-violence-expands-haiti-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens</link><description>
Armed gangs in Haiti control nearly all of Port-au-Prince and are expanding their reach outward. Once a peaceful farming community on the outskirts of the capital, the town of Kenscoff has found itself attacked again in recent days – violence that risks worsening food insecurity that the UN warns is already acute.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/533a246c-3c9f-11f0-81f0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25111850158844.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/533a246c-3c9f-11f0-81f0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25111850158844.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1128b9a4-813a-11f1-84ab-0f9c6cfc9d52</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 05:29:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/533a246c-3c9f-11f0-81f0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25111850158844.jpg">© AP/Odelyn Joseph</source><dc:creator>Zeenat Hansrod with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>France and England bosses say squads will take World Cup play off seriously</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260718-france-and-england-bosses-say-squads-will-take-world-cup-play-off-seriously</link><description>
France head coach Didier Deschamps and his England counterpart Thomas Tuchel say their teams will play Saturday's World Cup third place play-off game with intensity despite the disappointment of losing their semi-finals against Spain and Argentina respectively.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3764ea4-826e-11f1-86ce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/desss-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3764ea4-826e-11f1-86ce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/desss-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dac582e0-823b-11f1-ad48-0b87ea9fc21b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 06:16:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3764ea4-826e-11f1-86ce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/desss-1.jpg">AFP - CHANDAN KHANNA</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Syria taken off US terror blacklist after 47 years, paving way for investment</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260718-syria-taken-off-us-terror-blacklist-after-almost-47-years-paving-way-for-investment</link><description>
Syria is no longer designated a state sponsor of terrorism by the United States – a move that opens the door to American investment in the country, whose economy has been decimated by decades of conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e48e8298-7b30-11f1-b547-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T151203Z-1763665601-RC2R9MALPLGZ-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e48e8298-7b30-11f1-b547-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T151203Z-1763665601-RC2R9MALPLGZ-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5b9f81a2-7ba4-11f1-9a43-45851b99be57</guid><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 09:11:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e48e8298-7b30-11f1-b547-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-08T151203Z-1763665601-RC2R9MALPLGZ-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TRUMP.jpg">REUTERS - Jonathan Ernst</source><dc:creator>Anne-Marie Bissada</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>UK Labour party to crown 'King of the North' Burnham as leader and next PM</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260717-uk-labour-party-crowns-andy-burnham-as-leader-and-next-prime-minister</link><description>
The United Kingdom's  ruling Labour party will confirm veteran politician Andy Burnham as its new leader, and the country's next prime minister, at a special conference on Friday. He becomes the UK's seventh prime minister in a decade, replacing Keir Starmer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a82cdca-6bd9-11f1-9dde-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7MC6ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a82cdca-6bd9-11f1-9dde-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7MC6ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48b66fe4-81ab-11f1-8d4a-213d0dd984d3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 07:17:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a82cdca-6bd9-11f1-9dde-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7MC6ZR.jpg">AFP - OLI SCARFF</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>IEA report flags critical minerals risks as France steps up its strategy</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260717-iea-report-flags-critical-minerals-risks-as-france-steps-up-its-strategy</link><description>
The International Energy Agency has warned that investment in critical minerals fell in 2025 and supply chains grew more concentrated, posing fresh risks for France as it races to secure the raw materials needed for its industrial and energy transition.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/18e5cee8-dded-11f0-8d68-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-11-28T010256Z-1145778500-RC2C5IAM4N6D-RTRMADP-3-TECH-ARMS-CHINA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/18e5cee8-dded-11f0-8d68-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-11-28T010256Z-1145778500-RC2C5IAM4N6D-RTRMADP-3-TECH-ARMS-CHINA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c129216c-80f0-11f1-bbaf-73606c6dd95e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 13:06:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/18e5cee8-dded-11f0-8d68-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-11-28T010256Z-1145778500-RC2C5IAM4N6D-RTRMADP-3-TECH-ARMS-CHINA.jpg">REUTERS - CHINA STRINGER NETWORK</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's wheat production to fall after heatwaves push early harvest</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260717-france-s-wheat-production-drops-after-scorching-weather-pushes-early-harvest</link><description>
The wheat harvest in France, Europe’s largest grain producer, is expected to fall by 4 percent compared to 2025 after an unusually early harvest carried out during successive heatwaves.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbb520a-811f-11f1-b078-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T210149Z-1390557597-RC2C4MAG5N9F-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbb520a-811f-11f1-b078-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T210149Z-1390557597-RC2C4MAG5N9F-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e7d63f2-8120-11f1-a7de-6d02e2a4e797</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 08:28:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbb520a-811f-11f1-b078-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T210149Z-1390557597-RC2C4MAG5N9F-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg">© Stephane Mahe/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>UN campaign trail takes former president Macky Sall back to Senegal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260717-un-campaign-trail-takes-former-president-macky-sall-back-to-senegal</link><description>
Senegal's former president Macky Sall returns home on Friday for the first time since leaving office in April 2024, in a visit tied to his bid to become the next UN secretary-general. But opponents say the violence that marked the final months of his mandate should disqualify him from the role.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6048b00-8102-11f1-a9cf-e51ea97b6ed6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 05:05:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg">© REUTERS - Eduardo Munoz </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron toughens stance on arson, with dozens arrested as wildfires sweep France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-macron-toughens-stance-on-arson-as-wildfires-sweep-france</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron has said there would be "zero tolerance" for arson after France was hit by wildfires that have scorched thousands of hectares, as multiple heatwaves since May have dried out forests and fields. Dozens have been arrested across the country over starting fires, including a volunteer firefighter.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dbdc550e-8101-11f1-a945-6937b7331399</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 12:54:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">© Stéphane Mahe/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French teen sentenced to 18 years for fatal stabbing of school supervisor</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260717-french-teen-sentenced-to-18-years-for-fatal-stabbing-of-school-supervisor</link><description>
A French court on Thursday sentenced a 15-year-old boy to 18 years in prison for murdering a school supervisor outside his secondary school in the east of the country, citing his lack of "empathy, remorse or regret". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4794f14-46f5-11f0-92b1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-49WZ9K9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4794f14-46f5-11f0-92b1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-49WZ9K9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d12bc994-81b7-11f1-a3d9-a767334b21d9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 09:26:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4794f14-46f5-11f0-92b1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-49WZ9K9.jpg">AFP - FRANCOIS NASCIMBENI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>At least 20 children and one adult killed in school bus crash in Uganda</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260717-at-least-20-children-and-one-adult-killed-in-school-bus-crash-in-uganda</link><description>
At least 20 children and one adult have been killed after a bus carrying pupils home from a school trip crashed in eastern Uganda, police said on Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f7499d4-81c1-11f1-b93b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Uganda-schoolbus-accident.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f7499d4-81c1-11f1-b93b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Uganda-schoolbus-accident.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6e46cd20-81c5-11f1-a018-1f0843f75d2d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:52:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0f7499d4-81c1-11f1-b93b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Uganda-schoolbus-accident.jpg">© Uganda Police Force on X</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Fears over foreign influence in France, as Musk backs Le Pen presidential bid</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-elon-musk-s-backing-of-le-pen-presidential-bid-raises-foreign-influence-concerns-in-france</link><description>
Billionaire Elon Musk has thrown his support behind far-right leader Marine Le Pen's bid for the French presidency, calling her "France's last hope", and prompting accusations of foreign interference in the 2027 election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65867bc2-80f8-11f1-aac2-05c808138351</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 11:35:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg">© Mark Schiefelbein/AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French man charged with rape and murder of schoolgirl Lyhanna</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-french-man-charged-with-rape-murder-of-schoolgirl-lyhanna</link><description>
The main suspect in the death of an 11-year-old girl whose body was found in the Gers region has been charged with the rape and murder of a child. The case has sparked nationwide protests and renewed scrutiny of the French justice system, after it emerged that the suspect had previously been accused of raping another child.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bf726d0e-80e3-11f1-9ad7-11c429da1086</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 06:58:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg">© Julie Sebadelha/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Greenpeace Africa demands halt to $17bn Kenya coastal oil refinery</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260716-greenpeace-demands-halt-to-dangote-s-17bn-kenya-coastal-refinery</link><description>
Climate rights group Greenpeace Africa has called for a halt to a proposed oil refinery project by Africa's richest man, Aliko Dangote, in Kenya's coastal region, warning of the environmental risks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4ba7b34-8119-11f1-b689-57e3f657aba9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:29:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg">AFP - TONY KARUMBA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French parliament passes assisted dying law after years of wrangling</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-france-passes-assisted-dying-law-after-years-of-wrangling</link><description>
France's National Assembly has given its definitive backing to legislation granting terminally ill adults the right to end their lives with medical assistance, bringing to a close a protracted and often fraught political battle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">af51b17a-807d-11f1-90a2-95c1f2bcc31e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 06:10:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg">© REUTERS/Abdul Saboor</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Students in Cameroon protest new financial requirements for French visas</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260716-cameroonian-students-protest-new-french-visa-financial-rules</link><description>
Dozens of people took to the streets outside the French embassy in Yaoundé this week to protest new rules that require Cameroonian nationals to demonstrate the means to pay tuition fees in full before they can obtain a student visa for France. Protesters say the policy will make studying in France impossible for many people who already have places at French institutions for the coming academic year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7cab886-8028-11f1-95bb-a97de1dfa122</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 11:56:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg">© RFI / Emmanuel Jules Ntap</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU and Ukraine seal drone deal to pair industry with battlefield expertise</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260715-eu-ukraine-agree-drone-deal-to-pair-industry-with-battlefield-expertise</link><description>
European Union chief Ursula von der Leyen on Wednesday announced a drone deal with Ukraine to boost joint production of the key battlefield technology. 
